    "title": "NASA Artemis II Splashdown: Time, Live Stream and How to Watch Landing - The New York Times",
    "text": "AdvertisementSKIP ADVERTISEMENT See more of our coverage in your search results.Encuentra más de nuestra cobertura en los resultados de búsqueda. Add The New York Times on GoogleAgrega The New York Times en Google Splashdown Complete Distance from Moon 248,696 mi Source: NASA AROW. After venturing farther into space than anyone in history, four astronauts on NASA’s Artemis II are set to splash down in the Pacific Ocean off San Diego on Friday.The Orion spacecraft will bring Reid Wiseman, Victor Glover and Christina Koch of NASA and Jeremy Hansen of the Canadian Space Agency back home after 10 days and a trip around the far side of the moon.The splashdown ends the first crewed mission into deep space in more than 50 years. It is a significant step toward further space exploration and a new lunar landing.Here’s what you need to know about Artemis II and its splashdown.When is the splashdown, and how can I watch it?The crew is scheduled to splash down in the Pacific Ocean at approximately 8:07 p.m. Eastern time.AdvertisementSKIP ADVERTISEMENTNASA will stream video of the spacecraft’s return to Earth starting at 6:30 p.m. Friday. You can watch it on NASA’s YouTube and X accounts, as well as NASA’s website and smart TV apps. You can also watch it here on The New York Times’s website.You can track the Orion capsule’s speed and distance from Earth on NASA’s AROW website. It shows a visualization of the capsule.Subscribe to The Times to read as many articles as you like.Ashley Ahn covers breaking news for The Times from New York.See more on: National Aeronautics and Space AdministrationRead 59 commentsShare full article59Related ContentAdvertisementSKIP ADVERTISEMENTSupport independent journalism with a subscription. Already a subscriber? Log in.Enjoy unlimited access for $1 a week.Welcome offer$7.50 $1/weekBilled as $4 every four weeks for your first six months, then $30 thereafter. Continue with cardPayPalCancel or pause anytime.All Access includes news, plus Games, Cooking, Audio, Wirecutter and The Athletic.Offer for a New York Times All Access subscription. Current subscribers and those who have previously accepted a sale/introductory offer from The New York Times may be ineligible for another sale/introductory offer. Subscription excludes print edition. Some games may be available without a subscription. You will be automatically charged in advance $4.00 every 4 weeks for 6 months, and $30.00 every 4 weeks thereafter. Cancel before October 29, 2026 to avoid the transition to the standard price that will be charged on that date. You can cancel prior to renewal from your account settings online or during limited hours via chat or phone. Cancellation is effective at the end of the current billing period unless an exception applies; see our Terms of Sale. For U.S. subscribers, cancellation takes effect at the end of your current billing period. For international subscribers, see our Terms of Sale for further information. Taxes may apply. Offer terms are subject to change.©2026 The New York Times CompanyHelp Feedback",
